				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				685,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): align provider selector format and add language inference\n\nFix the provider registration and lookup chain:\n- Update CocoonService.RegisterProvider to use canonical selector format [{ \"language\": ... }] matching ProviderLookup's expectations\n- Change SideCarIdentifier to always route to \"cocoon-main\" instead of extension_id, enabling FeatureMethods to invoke providers correctly\n- Add language inference fallback in ProviderLookup: if document not in open state, derive language from file extension (.rs→rust, .ts→typescript, etc.)\n\nThis resolves provider lookup failures for language features like hover, completion, etc.",
			"SHA": "e7f2b53d37d580fd8027acb72a7c067eca7170ce"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T07:38:26Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				685,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): implement navigation history state and IPC handlers\n\nAdd NavigationHistoryState to track editor navigation stack (back/forward). This module provides a cursor-based navigation stack where Index points to the current position: GoBack decrements the index, GoForward increments it, and pushing a new entry truncates forward history.\n\nAlso adds IPC handlers to WindServiceHandlers:\n- Navigation history: goBack, goForward, canGoBack, canGoForward, push, clear, getStack\n- Label resolution: getUri, getWorkspace, getBase (human-readable display labels for URIs)\n- Text model registry: open, close, get, getAll, updateContent (document state management)\n\nThese handlers integrate with the Wind UI service layer to provide complete navigation and document management capabilities for the editor.",
			"SHA": "ee41bafb82d5ba159327231afac6946dab628182"
		}
	],
